<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nur al-Din Umar ibn Rasul</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1229">1229</a>–<a href="/years/1250">1250</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as al-Mansur Umar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> Umar ibn Rasul was a commander of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> origin who founded the Rasulid dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. Left as deputy when the last Ayyubid ruler departed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 1229, he soon declared independence, took the title al-Mansur and obtained recognition from the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. He ruled most of Yemen until he was murdered by his own mamluks in 1250.</p></div>
